     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. At least 75 NHRC staffs are trained and develop their capacity to link SDG and Human Rights. 
2. At least 50 law enforcement officials trained on Human Rights.
3. UPR report developed. 
4. National conference on business and human rights conducted</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	Conducted gender equality assessment at NHRC and developed institutional gender policies at NHRC accompanying an implementation plan which supported NHRC in developing affirmative action on GESI to better institutionalize its work on gender equality and social inclusion. 
&#x2022;	Trained a total of 181 conflict affect victims including 110 women of seven provinces on psychosocial counselling and mental health that geared up collaboration of victims to raise their voice in advocacy and lobby underscoring the issue of mental health;  provided the opportunity to conflict affected group and people discuss more on key issues, challenges and opportunities related to justice to transitional justice.
&#x2022;	Substantively digitalized NHRCs paper-based approach in complaint handling by developing online portal, SMS system, and upgrading these digital systems to replace paper-based complaint receiving into new innovation by developing NHRCs mobile app and setting up video conferencing system at its central, provincial and branch offices.
&#x2022;	Fielded NHRCs strong collaboration, coordination and leveraged its work among stakeholders, human rights academician, human rights defenders, parliamentarians, and international NHRIs through development and dissemination of ten of human rights promotional materials, human situation report and training manual to media persons and journalists.
&#x2022;	Excelled NHRCs outreach in raising public awareness, human rights monitoring and reporting during the pandemic to ensure citizens human rights by conducting human rights response against Ongoing Pandemic COVID-19 through reviewing laws related to crisis and disaster from social security and human rights perspective, broadcasting human rights PSA through local 34 FM stations in 14 local language, and supporting NHRCs human rights monitoring network in 77 district in collaboration with CSOs.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
